            ["do.add-hits"] = new BoardActionDef("do.add-hits", "Give a seat extra hits in the battle being fought, on top of its roll (Overcharge, Perfection, Twilight, Stains). Extra hits are not capped by a Vagabond's max hits, like Root's other extra hits.", "void AddHits(SeatId seat, int hits)", true, "After the roll, deal the extra hit as a separate one-hit removal through Root's own hit allocation (the owner of the hit pieces chooses), before hook.battle-resolved reads the result."),
            ["do.add-max-hits"] = new BoardActionDef("do.add-max-hits", "Raise a Vagabond's max hits (normally its undamaged swords) for the battle being fought (Belly Bounce: the Bag counts as one undamaged sword).", "void AddMaxHits(SeatId vagabond, int extra)", true, "If max hits cannot be changed, give one extra hit (do.add-hits) only when his roll was higher than his undamaged swords, which has the same effect."),
            ["do.ignore-first-hit"] = new BoardActionDef("do.ignore-first-hit", "Make a seat's warriors in the battle's clearing ignore the first hit they take, like the Keepers' Devout Knights (the White-Haired Man's Unbeatable in Act I).", "void IgnoreFirstHit(SeatId seat)", false, "After the battle, return one removed warrior of that seat to the clearing from its supply (do.place-warriors), which nets out the first hit. If do.place-warriors is also unavailable, Unbeatable in Act I is left out; it is flavour only, since no themed win is possible in Act I."),
            ["do.set-guard-floor"] = new BoardActionDef("do.set-guard-floor", "Keep at least this many of the host's warriors in a clearing: Root's move generator, its AI and the human UI may not move the host below the floor. 0 lifts it. Only a count: the host's other warriors come and go freely.", "void SetGuardFloor(SeatId host, ClearingId c, int floor)", true, "Esquie's no-spawn fallback (no guards, so no floor is needed)."),
